# Normalize to LF in the object database and on checkout, on every platform.
#
# This is the original setting, restored.  An earlier commit in this branch
# (fb1577b) replaced it with `-text` on the authoritative source paths, on the
# theory that the ledger's pinned SHA-256 values were hashes of CRLF bytes.
# They are not.  Measured on this tree, in binary mode:
#
#   src/XSSet.cpp                           174585 bytes, 0 CRLF, 4029 bare LF
#     sha256 0305496D2613C8D02668076F243CD856A61131B62B70978A96AC65B82C4D9FD5
#   tools/test_xe_reconstruct_fast_path.py     813 bytes, 0 CRLF,   22 bare LF
#     sha256 9735468FC6B751DC863485A205A73BEA07CFF27AD500125ABD8B0788A2BF6E41
#
# Both match GPU_RASBERRY_40X_OPTIMIZATION_LEDGER_20260820.md §3.2 exactly, so
# every pinned hash in the ledger is a hash of LF bytes and `eol=lf` is what
# reproduces them.  Do not trust `grep -c $'\r'` under Git Bash to tell you
# otherwise -- it reports a hit on every line of an LF-only file.  Check with:
#
#   python -c "import sys;b=open(sys.argv[1],'rb').read();print(b.count(b'\r\n'))" FILE
#
# `-text` is also actively worse here: it makes the repository faithfully
# record a CRLF file if a Windows editor writes one, instead of normalizing it
# away.  That happened once to src/PPR.cpp during this branch's work and showed
# up as a 1,823-line diff for a six-line change.
* text=auto eol=lf
